# Tests that differ from the reference, one a line: the test's name, then
# the reason. tests/rom/run.py reports each as KNOWN, never as ok; a known
# test that starts passing is reported too, so this list is kept true.
#
# Every one below is interrupt latency (README.md, Time): the test latches
# the counters from an interrupt's handler while the main code runs fixed
# work (irq_fixed), polls (irq_entry) or waits in a loop past the frame's
# end (frame_clock), with no WAI, so what it reads is when the handler
# started. The 65816 starts it at the end of the instruction in progress;
# nativeshvc's C marks no instruction ends, so the handler starts at the
# clock the interrupt comes due (or the end of the access in progress):
# earlier, here by 1 to 20 dots. Before the C stopped marking instruction
# ends, every one of these matched to the dot.
